Cksum: the checksum the cksum utility prints, as a builtin with no fork. $(cksum text)
answers the checksum and the byte length joined by a dash, $(cksum.hex text) seven hex
digits of the checksum modulo 2^28, and the .file forms hash a path's bytes whole, so
$(cksum.file path) equals a shell's cksum over the same file. The text forms hash the
bytes make hands them, a define's value with its newlines, and the star forms read a
variable's dedented value under the usual rule. A file that cannot be read answers
empty with one warning. The one routine, amk_cksum, is the cksum algorithm as POSIX
gives it, not zlib's crc32, so a key spelled by the pipe cksum | awk comes out the same
from the builtin and no cache entry moves. cksum joins .FEATURES, so a makefile can
guard on it and keep the pipe for a stock make.

